First, determine Sophia’s fuel efficiency (miles per gallon).

\[
\text{Miles per gallon} = \frac{\text{Miles traveled}}{\text{Gallons used}}
= \frac{100\ \text{miles}}{4\ \text{gallons}}
= 25\ \text{miles per gallon}
\]

Next, find how many miles she can drive on a full tank.  
The tank holds 12 gallons, so:

\[
\text{Miles per full tank} = (\text{Miles per gallon}) \times (\text{Gallons in tank})
= 25\ \text{miles/gallon} \times 12\ \text{gallons}
= 300\ \text{miles}
\]

Answer: 300
